drafts.text:
@lilyraynyc is right. The AI crowd is rediscovering SEO basics and calling them new.

For a local electrician or plumber, "AI search optimization" mostly looks like this: a page per service, the towns you cover, real reviews, the same phone number everywhere.

Boring works.

@randfish asks if AI visibility is a waste of time.

For local trades, don't chase it as its own project. Do the work that helps everywhere: clear service pages, your license number, your service area, real reviews.

If ChatGPT picks you up, great. Google still will.
